@authToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/identity/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@skarbiec.local",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd!123"
}

### --- Accounts ---

### Create a Brokerage account (type 0 = Brokerage, 1 = Bonds, 2 = Bank; wrapper 0 = Regular, 1 = Ike, 2 = Ikze; 400 Validation.BankFieldsNotAllowed for a bank field or a non-PLN currency)
# @name createBrokerageAccount
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "XTB IKE",
  "type": 0,
  "wrapper": 1
}

### Create a Bonds account
# @name createBondsAccount
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Obligacje IKE",
  "type": 1,
  "wrapper": 1
}

### Create an account with a taken name (409 Conflict.DuplicateName)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "XTB IKE",
  "type": 0,
  "wrapper": 0
}

### List accounts (every account by name, archived included)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Get an account
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts/{{createBrokerageAccount.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Rename an account (type, wrapper and currency never change)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts/{{createBrokerageAccount.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "XTB IKE (renamed)"
}

### Deposit money into the account (its cash is the cashAssetId of the account; unit price is always 1, 400 Validation.InsufficientFunds if a Withdraw would leave the balance below zero on any day)
# @name accountDeposit
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{createBrokerageAccount.response.body.cashAssetId}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Deposit",
  "quantity": 5000,
  "unitPrice": 1,
  "date": "2026-08-18"
}

### Withdraw money from the account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{createBrokerageAccount.response.body.cashAssetId}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Withdraw",
  "quantity": 1000,
  "unitPrice": 1,
  "date": "2026-08-19"
}

### List the other accounts' money a transfer can go to, bank accounts included (a cash place balance is listed with cashPlaces=true)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/transfer-candidates?currency=PLN&assetClass=Cash&accountCash=true
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Transfer between two accounts (400 Validation.InsufficientFunds above the balance, 400 Validation.InvalidTransferCounterpart to the same account, 400 Validation.TransferCurrencyMismatch between currencies)
# @name accountTransfer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAssetId": "{{createBrokerageAccount.response.body.cashAssetId}}",
  "targetAssetId": "{{createBondsAccount.response.body.cashAssetId}}",
  "amount": 3000,
  "date": "2026-08-20"
}

### Delete the transfer between accounts (400 Validation.InsufficientFunds once the target spent the money)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/transfers/{{accountTransfer.response.body.transferId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### --- Bank accounts ---

### Create a current Bank account (variant 0 = Current, 1 = Savings; the wrapper must be 0 = Regular, else 400 Validation.WrapperNotAllowed; currency PLN, EUR or USD)
# @name createMbankAccount
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "mBank",
  "type": 2,
  "wrapper": 0,
  "currency": "PLN",
  "variant": 0,
  "bankName": "mBank",
  "annualInterestRatePercent": 0
}

### Create a savings Bank account
# @name createNestAccount
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Nest Oszczednosciowe",
  "type": 2,
  "wrapper": 0,
  "currency": "PLN",
  "variant": 1,
  "bankName": "Nest Bank",
  "annualInterestRatePercent": 5
}

### List the Bank accounts only (type=Bank)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts?type=Bank
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Change a Bank account's variant, bank and rate (the rate applies from the next unsettled month)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts/{{createNestAccount.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Nest Oszczednosciowe",
  "variant": 1,
  "bankName": "Nest Bank",
  "annualInterestRatePercent": 4
}

### Deposit into the savings Bank account (its money is the cashAssetId of the account)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{createNestAccount.response.body.cashAssetId}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Deposit",
  "quantity": 10000,
  "unitPrice": 1,
  "date": "2026-08-01"
}

### Preview the Bank account's next due interest month (400 Validation.InterestNotSupported for a non-Bank account, 409 Conflict.AccountArchived)
# @name bankInterestPreview
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts/{{createNestAccount.response.body.id}}/interest-preview
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Settle the previewed interest month
# @name settleBankInterest
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts/{{createNestAccount.response.body.id}}/interest-settlements
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "periodEnd": "{{bankInterestPreview.response.body.periodEnd}}",
  "grossInterest": {{bankInterestPreview.response.body.grossInterest}},
  "tax": {{bankInterestPreview.response.body.tax}}
}

### Undo the latest interest settlement
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts/{{createNestAccount.response.body.id}}/interest-settlements/{{settleBankInterest.response.body.settlementId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Transfer from a Bank account to a brokerage account (counts toward an IKE or IKZE contribution)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAssetId": "{{createNestAccount.response.body.cashAssetId}}",
  "targetAssetId": "{{createBrokerageAccount.response.body.cashAssetId}}",
  "amount": 3000,
  "date": "2026-08-20"
}

### Set the 2026 contribution limit of an IKE/IKZE account (400 Validation.ContributionLimitNotAllowed on a Regular one; PUT replaces it)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts/{{createBrokerageAccount.response.body.id}}/contribution-limits/2026
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 26000
}

### Read the account with its contribution of 2026 (year defaults to the current Europe/Warsaw year)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts/{{createBrokerageAccount.response.body.id}}?year=2026
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Remove the 2026 contribution limit (204, or 404 when none is set)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts/{{createBrokerageAccount.response.body.id}}/contribution-limits/2026
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Archive an account (409 Conflict.AccountNotEmpty while its cash or an asset in it holds a quantity; publishes nothing)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts/{{createBondsAccount.response.body.id}}/archive
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Add a bond to the archived account (409 Conflict.AccountArchived)
# Run right after the archive above.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/bonds
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": "{{createBondsAccount.response.body.id}}",
  "name": "EDO1036",
  "seriesCode": "EDO1036",
  "type": 5,
  "purchaseDate": "2026-10-01",
  "bondCount": 50,
  "purchasePricePerBond": 100.00,
  "firstPeriodRatePercent": 5.35,
  "marginPercent": 2.00,
  "earlyRedemptionFeePerBond": 3.00
}

### Restore an archived account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts/{{createBondsAccount.response.body.id}}/restore
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Delete an account (409 Conflict.AccountHasHistory while it holds an asset other than its cash or has a cash transaction; removes its cash and publishes AssetRemoved)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/accounts/{{createBrokerageAccount.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}


### --- Assets ---

### Add a Cash asset (400 Validation.UseCashPlaceEndpoints: Cash is a cash place's balance or an account's money)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetClass": "Cash",
  "name": "Wallet",
  "currency": "PLN"
}

### Add a market-valuation asset
# @name addAsset
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": "{{createBrokerageAccount.response.body.id}}",
  "assetClass": "Stock",
  "name": "Example stock",
  "currency": "USD",
  "instrumentId": "{{addCustomInstrument.response.body.id}}"
}

### List assets
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets?accountId={{createBrokerageAccount.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Get an asset
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addAsset.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Update an asset
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addAsset.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetClass": "Stock",
  "name": "Example stock (renamed)",
  "currency": "USD",
  "instrumentId": "{{addCustomInstrument.response.body.id}}"
}

### Archive an asset
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addAsset.response.body.id}}/archive
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Update the archived asset (409)
# Run right after the archive above.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addAsset.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetClass": "Stock",
  "name": "Renamed while archived",
  "currency": "USD",
  "instrumentId": "{{addCustomInstrument.response.body.id}}"
}

### Restore an archived asset
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addAsset.response.body.id}}/restore
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Remove an asset
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addAsset.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}


### --- Transactions ---

### Record a transaction (a stock Buy settles in its account's cash)
# @name recordTransaction
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addAsset.response.body.id}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Buy",
  "quantity": 1,
  "unitPrice": 100,
  "date": "2026-08-18"
}

### Record a Deposit on the stock (400 Validation.TransactionTypeNotAllowed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addAsset.response.body.id}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Deposit",
  "quantity": 1,
  "unitPrice": 100,
  "date": "2026-08-18"
}

### List transactions (paged)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addAsset.response.body.id}}/transactions?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Update a transaction
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addAsset.response.body.id}}/transactions/{{recordTransaction.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Buy",
  "quantity": 1,
  "unitPrice": 105,
  "date": "2026-08-18"
}

### Delete a transaction
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addAsset.response.body.id}}/transactions/{{recordTransaction.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}


### --- Term deposits ---

### Fund the mBank account (a deposit is always opened from a Bank account; the deposit takes its currency)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{createMbankAccount.response.body.cashAssetId}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Deposit",
  "quantity": 40000,
  "unitPrice": 1,
  "date": "2025-12-31"
}

### Add a term deposit from the mBank account (returnAccountId defaults to the source; 400 Validation.InsufficientFunds when the balance is short on any day, 400 Validation.BankAccountRequired for a non-Bank source)
# @name addDeposit
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "3-month deposit",
  "bankName": "Example bank",
  "sourceAccountId": "{{createMbankAccount.response.body.id}}",
  "principal": 10000.00,
  "startDate": "2026-01-15",
  "termLength": 3,
  "termUnit": 1,
  "annualInterestRatePercent": 6,
  "capitalization": 0,
  "earlyBreakInterestLossPercent": 100
}

### Add a term deposit that returns to the savings Bank account
# @name addFundedDeposit
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Funded deposit",
  "bankName": "Example bank",
  "sourceAccountId": "{{createMbankAccount.response.body.id}}",
  "returnAccountId": "{{createNestAccount.response.body.id}}",
  "principal": 1000.00,
  "startDate": "2026-01-15",
  "termLength": 3,
  "termUnit": 1,
  "annualInterestRatePercent": 6,
  "capitalization": 0,
  "earlyBreakInterestLossPercent": 100
}

### List every deposit
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### List the deposits a Bank account funds or receives
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits?accountId={{createMbankAccount.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Get a deposit
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits/{{addDeposit.response.body.assetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Update a deposit (the source is fixed; returnAccountId is optional and keeps the stored one when left out; a settled deposit not yet paid out accepts a returnAccountId change alone)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits/{{addDeposit.response.body.assetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "6-month deposit",
  "bankName": "Example bank",
  "returnAccountId": "{{createMbankAccount.response.body.id}}",
  "principal": 15000.00,
  "startDate": "2026-02-01",
  "termLength": 6,
  "termUnit": 1,
  "annualInterestRatePercent": 5.5,
  "capitalization": 2,
  "earlyBreakInterestLossPercent": 100
}

### Record a transaction on the deposit (409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addDeposit.response.body.assetId}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": 2,
  "quantity": 500,
  "unitPrice": 1,
  "date": "2026-02-01"
}

### Preview the settlement of a Due deposit
# @name settlementPreview
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits/{{addDeposit.response.body.assetId}}/settlement-preview
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Settle the deposit
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits/{{addDeposit.response.body.assetId}}/settle
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "settledOn": "{{settlementPreview.response.body.settledOn}}",
  "grossInterest": {{settlementPreview.response.body.grossInterest}},
  "tax": {{settlementPreview.response.body.tax}}
}

### Pay the settled deposit out to its return account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits/{{addDeposit.response.body.assetId}}/payout
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "{{settlementPreview.response.body.settledOn}}"
}

### Preview the settlement of the funded deposit
# @name fundedSettlementPreview
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits/{{addFundedDeposit.response.body.assetId}}/settlement-preview
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Settle the funded deposit and pay it out at once
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits/{{addFundedDeposit.response.body.assetId}}/settle
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "settledOn": "{{fundedSettlementPreview.response.body.settledOn}}",
  "grossInterest": {{fundedSettlementPreview.response.body.grossInterest}},
  "tax": {{fundedSettlementPreview.response.body.tax}},
  "payOut": true
}

### Add a matured deposit to roll over
# @name addRenewableDeposit
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Renewable deposit",
  "bankName": "Example bank",
  "sourceAccountId": "{{createMbankAccount.response.body.id}}",
  "principal": 10000.00,
  "startDate": "2026-01-15",
  "termLength": 3,
  "termUnit": 1,
  "annualInterestRatePercent": 6,
  "capitalization": 0,
  "earlyBreakInterestLossPercent": 100
}

### Preview the settlement of the renewable deposit
# @name renewablePreview
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits/{{addRenewableDeposit.response.body.assetId}}/settlement-preview
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Roll the Due deposit over
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits/{{addRenewableDeposit.response.body.assetId}}/rollover
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "annualInterestRatePercent": 5.5,
  "grossInterest": {{renewablePreview.response.body.grossInterest}},
  "tax": {{renewablePreview.response.body.tax}}
}

### Preview the settlement of the rolled-over term
# @name renewedPreview
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits/{{addRenewableDeposit.response.body.assetId}}/settlement-preview
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Settle the rolled-over term, keeping the money in the deposit
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits/{{addRenewableDeposit.response.body.assetId}}/settle
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "settledOn": "{{renewedPreview.response.body.settledOn}}",
  "grossInterest": {{renewedPreview.response.body.grossInterest}},
  "tax": {{renewedPreview.response.body.tax}}
}

### Roll the Settled deposit over
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits/{{addRenewableDeposit.response.body.assetId}}/rollover
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "annualInterestRatePercent": 5
}

### --- Treasury bonds ---

### Deposit money into the Bonds account's cash: every bond purchase, coupon, redemption and swap settles there
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{createBondsAccount.response.body.cashAssetId}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Deposit",
  "quantity": 20000,
  "unitPrice": 1,
  "date": "2026-01-01"
}

### Add a treasury bond paid from the account's cash (type 5 = EDO; 400 Validation.InsufficientFunds when the cash would go negative on any day)
# @name addBond
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/bonds
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": "{{createBondsAccount.response.body.id}}",
  "name": "EDO1036",
  "seriesCode": "EDO1036",
  "type": 5,
  "purchaseDate": "2026-10-01",
  "bondCount": 50,
  "purchasePricePerBond": 100.00,
  "firstPeriodRatePercent": 5.35,
  "marginPercent": 2.00,
  "earlyRedemptionFeePerBond": 3.00
}

### Add a second treasury bond (type 1 = ROR)
# @name addFundedBond
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/bonds
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": "{{createBondsAccount.response.body.id}}",
  "name": "ROR0627",
  "seriesCode": "ROR0627",
  "type": 1,
  "purchaseDate": "2026-06-10",
  "bondCount": 10,
  "purchasePricePerBond": 100.00,
  "firstPeriodRatePercent": 4.25,
  "earlyRedemptionFeePerBond": 0.50
}

### List every bond — each with estimate {grossValue, netValue, asOf} or null and estimateUnavailableReason (RateMissing | MarketDataUnavailable)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/bonds
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Get a bond
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/bonds/{{addBond.response.body.assetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Update a bond
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/bonds/{{addBond.response.body.assetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "EDO1036 (renamed)",
  "seriesCode": "EDO1036",
  "type": 5,
  "purchaseDate": "2026-10-01",
  "bondCount": 60,
  "purchasePricePerBond": 100.00,
  "firstPeriodRatePercent": 5.35,
  "marginPercent": 2.00,
  "earlyRedemptionFeePerBond": 3.00
}

### Record a transaction on the bond (409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addBond.response.body.assetId}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": 2,
  "quantity": 500,
  "unitPrice": 1,
  "date": "2026-10-01"
}

### Preview the funded ROR's three due months (period 1 takes the rate from the terms)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/bonds/{{addFundedBond.response.body.assetId}}/interest-settlements/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "periods": [
    { "periodIndex": 1 },
    { "periodIndex": 2, "ratePercent": 3.75 },
    { "periodIndex": 3, "ratePercent": 3.75 }
  ]
}

### Settle them: each net coupon is credited and moved Bond → account cash on its period end (400 Validation.InsufficientFunds when undoing a spent coupon)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/bonds/{{addFundedBond.response.body.assetId}}/interest-settlements
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "periods": [
    { "periodIndex": 1 },
    { "periodIndex": 2, "ratePercent": 3.75 },
    { "periodIndex": 3, "ratePercent": 3.75 }
  ]
}

### Get the funded ROR: settled periods, duePeriodCount and lastSettlement
# @name getFundedBond
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/bonds/{{addFundedBond.response.body.assetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Undo the latest settlement (only the latest can be undone)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/bonds/{{addFundedBond.response.body.assetId}}/interest-settlements/{{getFundedBond.response.body.lastSettlement.settlementId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Preview redeeming 4 of the funded ROR's 10 early, inside month 3 (months 1–2 stay settled after the undo)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/bonds/{{addFundedBond.response.body.assetId}}/early-redemption-preview?date=2026-09-05&bondCount=4&runningPeriodRatePercent=3.75
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Redeem them early: accrued interest credited, the full fee and Belka tax charged, the proceeds moved Bond → account cash; 6 bonds remain
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/bonds/{{addFundedBond.response.body.assetId}}/early-redemption
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-09-05",
  "bondCount": 4,
  "runningPeriodRatePercent": 3.75
}

### Add a matured 3-month bond (type 0 = OTS)
# @name addMaturedBond
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/bonds
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": "{{createBondsAccount.response.body.id}}",
  "name": "OTS0926",
  "seriesCode": "OTS0926",
  "type": 0,
  "purchaseDate": "2026-06-01",
  "bondCount": 10,
  "purchasePricePerBond": 100.00,
  "firstPeriodRatePercent": 3.00,
  "earlyRedemptionFeePerBond": 0.00
}

### Settle its only period: the interest is capitalised into the bond
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/bonds/{{addMaturedBond.response.body.assetId}}/interest-settlements
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "periods": [
    { "periodIndex": 1 }
  ]
}

### Preview its redemption: capitalised interest, discount, Belka tax and proceeds, all dated the maturity date
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/bonds/{{addMaturedBond.response.body.assetId}}/redemption-preview
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Swap 6 of the 10 into a new series at the swap price; the rest of the proceeds goes to the account cash, and a swap costing more than the proceeds takes the shortfall from it (400 Validation.InsufficientFunds when it cannot cover it; send the redemption below instead to pay everything out)
# @name swapBond
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/bonds/{{addMaturedBond.response.body.assetId}}/swap
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bondCount": 6,
  "newBond": {
    "name": "EDO0936",
    "seriesCode": "EDO0936",
    "type": 5,
    "swapPricePerBond": 99.90,
    "firstPeriodRatePercent": 5.35,
    "marginPercent": 2.00,
    "earlyRedemptionFeePerBond": 3.00
  }
}

### Redeem the whole holding to the account cash instead (409 once it was swapped)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/bonds/{{addMaturedBond.response.body.assetId}}/redemption
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Get the redeemed bond: status Redeemed, its redemption and the swap target's name
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/bonds/{{addMaturedBond.response.body.assetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### --- Cash places ---

### Create a cash place with a balance per currency (PLN, EUR, USD; PLN alone when omitted; 409 Conflict.DuplicateName)
# @name createCashPlace
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/cash-places
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sejf",
  "currencies": ["PLN", "USD"]
}

### Add a currency balance (409 Conflict.DuplicateCurrency, 409 Conflict.CashPlaceArchived)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/cash-places/{{createCashPlace.response.body.id}}/currencies
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### Deposit 2000 PLN from outside into the place's PLN balance (its cashAssetId; 400 Validation.InsufficientFunds when a Withdraw would leave it below zero on any day)
# @name cashPlaceDeposit
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{createCashPlace.response.body.$.balances[0].cashAssetId}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Deposit",
  "quantity": 2000,
  "unitPrice": 1,
  "date": "2026-10-01"
}

### ATM withdrawal: bank money (mBank) into the place's PLN balance (400 Validation.TransferCurrencyMismatch between currencies, 400 Validation.InvalidTransferCounterpart place to place or to a brokerage account's cash)
# @name atmWithdrawal
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAssetId": "{{createMbankAccount.response.body.cashAssetId}}",
  "targetAssetId": "{{createCashPlace.response.body.$.balances[0].cashAssetId}}",
  "amount": 500,
  "date": "2026-10-05"
}

### Bank deposit: the place's PLN balance into the bank money
# @name bankDeposit
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAssetId": "{{createCashPlace.response.body.$.balances[0].cashAssetId}}",
  "targetAssetId": "{{createMbankAccount.response.body.cashAssetId}}",
  "amount": 200,
  "date": "2026-10-06"
}

### Delete the bank deposit
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/transfers/{{bankDeposit.response.body.transferId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### List the place balances a transfer can go to, in a currency
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/transfer-candidates?currency=PLN&cashPlaces=true
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### List every place with balances valued in PLN at the latest rate, and totals per currency (fxUnavailable with null foreign values when MarketData is down)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/cash-places
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Get a place
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/cash-places/{{createCashPlace.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Rename a place and its balances
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/cash-places/{{createCashPlace.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sejf domowy"
}

### Archive a place (409 Conflict.CashPlaceNotEmpty while a balance is not 0; any later write is 409 Conflict.CashPlaceArchived)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/cash-places/{{createCashPlace.response.body.id}}/archive
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Restore a place
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/cash-places/{{createCashPlace.response.body.id}}/restore
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Delete a place (409 Conflict.CashPlaceHasHistory once a balance has a transaction; publishes AssetRemoved per balance)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/cash-places/{{createCashPlace.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### List Stock holdings, with value in PLN and unrealised gain — assetClass=Stock|Etf
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/securities?assetClass=Stock
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### List ETF holdings
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/securities?assetClass=Etf
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Watch an instrument, with an optional note and target price
# @name addWatchlistItem
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/watchlist
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "instrumentId": "{{addCustomInstrument.response.body.id}}",
  "note": "Buy on a dip",
  "targetPrice": 100
}

### List the watchlist with prices, daily change and holdings — optional assetClass=Stock|Etf
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/watchlist
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Get a watchlist item
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/watchlist/{{addWatchlistItem.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Replace a watchlist item's note and target price (null clears one)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/watchlist/{{addWatchlistItem.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "note": null,
  "targetPrice": 95.5
}

### Remove a watchlist item
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/watchlist/{{addWatchlistItem.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### --- Paying a deposit out into a bank account ---

### Add a matured deposit that returns to the savings Bank account (400 Validation.TransferCurrencyMismatch for a return account in another currency)
# @name addBankBoundDeposit
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Deposit for the bank account",
  "bankName": "Example bank",
  "sourceAccountId": "{{createMbankAccount.response.body.id}}",
  "returnAccountId": "{{createNestAccount.response.body.id}}",
  "principal": 10000.00,
  "startDate": "2026-01-15",
  "termLength": 3,
  "termUnit": 1,
  "annualInterestRatePercent": 6,
  "capitalization": 0,
  "earlyBreakInterestLossPercent": 100
}

### Preview the settlement of the deposit bound for the bank account
# @name bankBoundPreview
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits/{{addBankBoundDeposit.response.body.assetId}}/settlement-preview
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Settle the deposit and pay it out to its return account at once
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/deposits/{{addBankBoundDeposit.response.body.assetId}}/settle
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "settledOn": "{{bankBoundPreview.response.body.settledOn}}",
  "grossInterest": {{bankBoundPreview.response.body.grossInterest}},
  "tax": {{bankBoundPreview.response.body.tax}},
  "payOut": true
}

### --- Precious metals ---

### Create a cash place to pay metals from (its PLN balance is the cashAssetId)
# @name addFundingCash
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/cash-places
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Metals cash",
  "currencies": ["PLN"]
}

### Fund the metals cash place
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addFundingCash.response.body.$.balances[0].cashAssetId}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Deposit",
  "quantity": 5000,
  "unitPrice": 1,
  "date": "2026-01-01"
}

### Add a silver coin with a first purchase (metal 1 = Silver; weightUnit Gram | TroyOunce)
# @name addMetal
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/metals
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Maple Leaf 1 oz",
  "metal": 1,
  "fineWeight": 1,
  "weightUnit": "TroyOunce",
  "firstPurchase": {
    "pieces": 10,
    "pricePerPiece": 260.00,
    "date": "2026-10-01"
  }
}

### Add a gold bar with no purchase yet (metal 0 = Gold)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/metals
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Gold bar 50 g",
  "metal": 0,
  "fineWeight": 50,
  "weightUnit": "Gram"
}

### List every precious metal holding
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/metals
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Get a precious metal holding
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/metals/{{addMetal.response.body.assetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Update it: metal, name and fine weight (moves the instrument with the metal)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/metals/{{addMetal.response.body.assetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Silver bar 100 g",
  "metal": 1,
  "fineWeight": 100,
  "weightUnit": "Gram"
}

### Buy one more piece (a PreciousMetal asset takes Buy and Sell only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addMetal.response.body.assetId}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": 0,
  "quantity": 1,
  "unitPrice": 270.00,
  "date": "2026-10-02"
}

### Buy one piece paid from the metals cash place: a linked Cash Withdraw of quantity × unitPrice
# @name metalBuyWithCash
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addMetal.response.body.assetId}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": 0,
  "quantity": 1,
  "unitPrice": 275.00,
  "date": "2026-10-03",
  "cashAssetId": "{{addFundingCash.response.body.$.balances[0].cashAssetId}}"
}

### Sell one piece into the metals cash place: a linked Cash Deposit of quantity × unitPrice
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addMetal.response.body.assetId}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": 1,
  "quantity": 1,
  "unitPrice": 280.00,
  "date": "2026-10-04",
  "cashAssetId": "{{addFundingCash.response.body.$.balances[0].cashAssetId}}"
}

### Add a PLN stock to trade through its account's cash (deposit into the account first)
# @name addPlnStock
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": "{{createBrokerageAccount.response.body.id}}",
  "assetClass": "Stock",
  "name": "PLN stock",
  "currency": "PLN",
  "instrumentId": "{{addCustomInstrument.response.body.id}}"
}

### Buy 10 shares with a 3 zł fee: a linked Withdraw from the account's cash of round(quantity x unitPrice x rate, 2) + fee (400 Validation.InsufficientFunds when the cash would go negative on any day, 400 Validation.CashLinkNotAllowed with a cashAssetId)
# @name stockBuy
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addPlnStock.response.body.id}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Buy",
  "quantity": 10,
  "unitPrice": 120.00,
  "date": "2026-10-05",
  "feeAmount": 3.00
}

### Sell 4 shares: a linked Deposit into the account's cash of the gross less the fee (400 Validation.FeeExceedsProceeds when the fee is higher)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addPlnStock.response.body.id}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Sell",
  "quantity": 4,
  "unitPrice": 130.00,
  "date": "2026-10-06",
  "feeAmount": 3.00
}

### Buy 2 shares of the USD stock: the cash leg is a PLN Withdraw at the USDPLN rate of the day (400 Validation.FxRateMissing when MarketData has none that early)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addAsset.response.body.id}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Buy",
  "quantity": 2,
  "unitPrice": 100.00,
  "date": "2026-10-05",
  "feeAmount": 5.00
}

### Buy 2 shares of the USD stock paid in PLN: amountPln is what the broker charged without the fee, it sets the rate (amountPln / (quantity x unitPrice)) and the cash leg (amountPln + fee); no MarketData call (400 Validation.PlnAmountNotAllowed on a PLN asset, a Dividend or a non-positive amount)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addAsset.response.body.id}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Buy",
  "quantity": 2,
  "unitPrice": 100.00,
  "date": "2026-10-05",
  "feeAmount": 5.00,
  "amountPln": 812.00
}

### Record a dividend: the quantity is the net PLN amount (unit price 1, FX 1), paid into the account's cash at any position size
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addPlnStock.response.body.id}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Dividend",
  "quantity": 37.40,
  "unitPrice": 1,
  "date": "2026-10-07"
}

### Update the buy: the cash leg is resized and the rate re-frozen for the new date
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets/{{addPlnStock.response.body.id}}/transactions/{{stockBuy.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Buy",
  "quantity": 10,
  "unitPrice": 110.00,
  "date": "2026-10-05",
  "feeAmount": 3.00
}

### Delete the funded buy: both legs go (409 Conflict.OversellsPosition if a later Sell needs its pieces)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/transfers/{{metalBuyWithCash.response.body.transfer.transferId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Add a precious metal through the generic assets endpoint (400 Validation.UseMetalEndpoints)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio/assets
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetClass": 6,
  "name": "Gold coin",
  "currency": "PLN",
  "instrumentId": "{{addCustomInstrument.response.body.id}}"
}
